menu "Micro OS image"

    config MICRO_OS_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE
        bool "refuse an image without a valid signature"
        default y
        help
            The application checks the trailer of its own factory partition
            (MOSIGN01, SHA-256 and Ed25519) at the beginning of app_main,
            before the filesystem and the shell. On, an image without a valid
            trailer prints the reason and stops the boot; off, the check is
            still made and the line
            "unsigned or damaged image: not guaranteed" goes to the console,
            and the board continues. The check is electronic: the ROM and the
            ESP-IDF bootloader have already loaded the application, so a
            damaged image may have run its first instructions before the
            sentence appears. The board bundle is signed by tools/bundle.sh,
            and the public key is compiled into the firmware.

    config MICRO_OS_ANTIROLLBACK
        bool "refuse an image older than the version stored in the NVS"
        default n
        help
            The version of the image comes from esp_app_desc_t.version. The
            boot keeps the newest version it has seen in the NVS and refuses
            a lower one (prints the two versions and stops) when this flag is
            on; with the flag off a rollback is a warning. The minimum is
            updated after a signature that passed. The store is the NVS of
            the board, not /etc: the check runs before the filesystem is
            mounted. This is not the secure-boot anti-rollback of the eFuses
            and it does not protect the NVS from a person who can flash the
            board.

endmenu
